<%# The context a newcomer needs first: what Mayo Irish is and where it is
    spoken, in the same terms as lesson 0 of the Mayo Irish course. %>
<section class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl px-4 py-8 mx-auto space-y-12 lg:space-y-20 lg:py-24 lg:px-6">
    <div class="items-center gap-8 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 xl:gap-16" data-controller="map" data-map-pins-value="<%= @pins.to_json %>">
      <div class="text-gray-500 sm:text-lg dark:text-gray-400">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white">The Irish of Mayo</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 font-light lg:text-xl">Most courses and dictionaries follow Connemara Irish or the standard. The speakers here come from Erris, Achill, Tourmakeady and east Mayo, and from the neighbouring districts where Irish was once spoken.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 font-light lg:text-xl">Irish is still a community language in three Mayo Gaeltacht areas: <strong>Erris, Achill and Tourmakeady</strong>. In the 2022 census about 10,500 people lived in the Mayo Gaeltacht, 5,956 of them said they could speak Irish, and 555 spoke it every day outside school (<a class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline" href="https://www.cso.ie/en/csolatestnews/pressreleases/2023pressreleases/pressstatementcensus2022resultsprofile8-theirishlanguageandeducationmayo">CSO</a>).</p>
        <p class="mb-8 font-light lg:text-xl">A century ago far more of the county spoke it. <a class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline" href="/1926">Find your own parish on the 1926 Gaeltacht map</a> to see how it was classed then.</p>
        <p class="hidden font-medium text-gray-900 lg:block dark:text-white">Click on the map to listen to speakers from all over Mayo and follow the links to their recordings, words and phrases.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hidden w-full mb-4 rounded-lg lg:mb-0 lg:flex" data-map-target="desktopContainer">
        <div id="map" class="w-full h-[450px]"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white">How the dialects divide</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
        <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Tuaisceart Mhaigh Eo</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">Erris and the north-west of the county. Still a Gaeltacht.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Acaill</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">Achill and the coast around it. Still a Gaeltacht. Like Erris, it shares a good deal of vocabulary and pronunciation with Ulster Irish.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Lár Chonnachta</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">South Mayo, including Tourmakeady, with most of Roscommon and north and east Galway. Tourmakeady is still a Gaeltacht.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Connachta ó Thuaidh</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">North-east Mayo, Sligo and the north of Roscommon and Leitrim. Irish has died out here as a community language, but recordings of its last speakers survive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">The divisions follow Tomás Ó Máille's account of Connacht Irish as it stood in 1927.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
  <div class="items-center max-w-screen-xl px-4 py-8 mx-auto lg:grid lg:grid-cols-4 lg:gap-16 xl:gap-24 lg:py-24 lg:px-6">
    <div class="col-span-2 mb-8">
      <video class="w-full mb-4 rounded-lg lg:mb-0 lg:flex" controls preload="none" poster="https://assets.abairt.com/darren.png" aria-label="Darren Ó Riagáin, a non-native speaker, speaking Irish">
        <source src="https://assets.abairt.com/darren-reagan-bofield.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
    </div>
    <div class="col-span-2 space-y-8 md:grid md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12 md:space-y-0">
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold dark:text-white"><%= number_with_delimiter(@stats[:recordings]) %> recordings</h3>
        <p class="font-light text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Interviews, stories, songs, transcribed line by line.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold dark:text-white"><%= number_with_delimiter(@stats[:speakers]) %> native speakers</h3>
        <p class="font-light text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">From across the Mayo dialects.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold dark:text-white"><%= number_with_delimiter(@stats[:phrases]) %> words and phrases</h3>
        <p class="font-light text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Folca, seanráite, seanchas, abairtí.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold dark:text-white"><%= number_with_delimiter(@stats[:with_audio]) %> with audio</h3>
        <p class="font-light text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Words and phrases you can hear as well as read.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl px-4 py-8 mx-auto space-y-12 lg:space-y-20 lg:py-24 lg:px-6">
    <div class="items-center gap-8 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 xl:gap-16">
      <video class="w-full mb-4 rounded-lg lg:mb-0 lg:flex" controls preload="none" poster="https://assets.abairt.com/transcription-demo-poster.png" aria-label="Demonstration of the transcription tools">
        <source src="https://assets.abairt.com/transcription-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
      <div class="text-gray-500 sm:text-lg dark:text-gray-400">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Listen, read, search</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 font-light lg:text-xl">Every recording has a transcript you can follow as it plays, in Irish or English.</p>
        <ul role="list" class="pt-8 space-y-5 border-t border-gray-200 my-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <%= render "home/point", text: "Toggle Irish and English subtitles, or export them" %>
          <%= render "home/point", text: "Slow down, isolate and loop any passage" %>
          <%= render "home/point", text: "Full text search in Irish and English" %>
          <%= render "home/point", text: "Filter by speaker, dialect, tag and location" %>
          <%= render "home/point", text: "Find pubs and other places where Irish is spoken in public" %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="learn" class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl px-4 py-8 mx-auto lg:py-24 lg:px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Learning Irish?</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 font-light text-gray-500 sm:text-lg lg:text-xl dark:text-gray-400">
        Abairt is the collection. For structured lessons, there is the <strong>Mayo Irish course</strong>: Mícheál Ó Siadhail's <em>Learning Irish</em>, adapted lesson by lesson for the Irish of Mayo, with the speakers you hear on Abairt.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-8 font-light text-gray-500 sm:text-lg dark:text-gray-400">
        It is free, and invite-only while it is being built.
      </p>
      <%= link_to "Go to the Mayo Irish course", @course_url, class: "inline-flex items-center justify-center px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-center text-white bg-blue-500 border border-blue-500 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 focus:ring-4 focus:ring-blue-300 dark:border-gray-700 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 dark:focus:ring-gray-800" %>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
        The best way to learn is still to spend time among native speakers, in the Gaeltacht or with a speaker who becomes a friend. Use what is here alongside that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl px-4 py-8 mx-auto lg:py-24 lg:px-6">
    <div class="text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Where the recordings come from</h2>
      <p class="font-light text-gray-500 sm:text-lg lg:text-xl dark:text-gray-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        Community contributions and automated processing, checked by native speakers.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 mb-4 bg-purple-100 rounded-lg dark:bg-purple-900">
          <span class="text-lg font-semibold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-300">1</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Collect</h3>
        <p class="font-light">Native speakers and community members upload recordings, and a nightly import brings in Irish-language media, mostly from <a class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline" href="https://turassiar.ie/">Turas Siar</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 mb-4 bg-green-100 rounded-lg dark:bg-green-900">
          <span class="text-lg font-semibold text-green-600 dark:text-green-300">2</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Process</h3>
        <p class="font-light">Each recording is split by speaker, transcribed with <a class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline" href="https://abair.ie">ABAIR</a>'s speech recognition and given a draft English translation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md dark:bg-gray-900">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 mb-4 bg-blue-100 rounded-lg dark:bg-blue-900">
          <span class="text-lg font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-300">3</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Check</h3>
        <p class="font-light">Native speakers correct the transcripts and translations, and add speakers and places. Only checked entries are confirmed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-center text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      Are you a native speaker or a fluent Irish speaker?
      <%= link_to "Sign up", new_registration_path, class: "text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline font-medium" %> to help check recordings.
      Building something? There is an <%= link_to "open API", api_docs_path, class: "text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline font-medium" %>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl px-4 py-8 mx-auto text-center lg:py-24 lg:px-6">
    <figure class="max-w-screen-md mx-auto">
      <svg class="h-12 mx-auto mb-3 text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600" viewBox="0 0 24 27" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M14.017 18L14.017 10.609C14.017 4.905 17.748 1.039 23 0L23.995 2.151C21.563 3.068 20 5.789 20 8H24V18H14.017ZM0 18V10.609C0 4.905 3.748 1.038 9 0L9.996 2.151C7.563 3.068 6 5.789 6 8H9.983L9.983 18L0 18Z" fill="currentColor"/>
      </svg>
      <blockquote>
        <p class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-900 md:text-2xl dark:text-white">"An chéad chainteoir eile, 'the next speaker'. The goal of this site is to increase the number of adult speakers in the community."</p>
      </blockquote>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl px-4 pb-8 mx-auto lg:pb-24 lg:px-6">
    <h2 id="faq" class="mb-6 p-6 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-center text-gray-900 lg:mb-8 lg:text-3xl dark:text-white">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="max-w-screen-md mx-auto">
      <%= render "home/faq_item", question: "Is Abairt free?" do %>
        <p>Yes. The aim is a high-quality collection of native Irish speech that anyone can use, and we don't want money to stand in the way.</p>
        <p>Abairt is not run for commercial gain and has no analytics or tracking. If you sign up, your email is used for login and notifications, nothing else.</p>
        <p>We make no claim on the material. It is shared freely, and the copyright and licensing belong to the owners of the original recordings.</p>
        <p>You are welcome to <a href="https://github.com/seocahill/abairt" class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline">fork the code</a> and build a community of your own.</p>
      <% end %>
      <%= render "home/faq_item", question: "Do I need to sign up?" do %>
        <p><strong>No.</strong> Everything you can listen to, read and search is open. Sign up if you want to help check and improve recordings.</p>
      <% end %>
      <%= render "home/faq_item", question: "How do I get the most from the recordings?" do %>
        <ul class="pl-5 space-y-2 list-disc">
          <li><strong>Start with the map</strong> to hear speakers from different areas and notice how the Irish changes.</li>
          <li><strong>Search</strong> for a word or phrase in Irish or English to hear it in context.</li>
          <li><strong>Slow it down and loop it</strong> until you can copy the sounds and the rhythm.</li>
          <li><strong>Read along</strong> with Irish or English subtitles to follow the meaning.</li>
        </ul>
      <% end %>
      <%= render "home/faq_item", question: "Is the transcription always right?" do %>
        <p>Not always. Transcripts and translations start as machine drafts and are corrected by native speakers; entries marked as confirmed have been checked.</p>
        <p>The speech services come from <a class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline" href="https://abair.ie">ABAIR</a> and are not always available. <%= link_to "Check their status", status_path, class: "text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline" %> if something isn't working.</p>
      <% end %>
      <%= render "home/faq_item", question: "Found a problem?" do %>
        <p>Please <a href="https://github.com/seocahill/abairt/issues" class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-500 hover:underline">report it on GitHub</a>. Abairt runs on modest infrastructure, so it may occasionally be slow or briefly down.</p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

